DEBUG 2026-05-13 14:33:06,975 views 23778 127131090679488 [REQUEST RAW] {"message":"give me a summary","page":"/","pageTitle":"Kenya Cultural Heritage - Explore Top 10 Communities","url":"http://localhost:8080/","selectedText":"tell me something intresting about somali communiyy\n\n02:25 PM\n\n{ \"type\": \"message\", \"content\": \"One interesting aspect of the Somali community is their rich tradition of storytelling and oral poetry, known as 'Hees'. Hees is a unique form of Somali literature that has been passed down through generations, often recited during social gatherings, weddings, and other important events. In Hees, Somali poets and storytellers use intricate rhymes, metaphors, and wordplay to convey complex emotions, historical events, and cultural values. Hees is not just a form of entertainment but also serves as a way to preserve Somali history, culture, and identity. The Somali people have a deep appreciation for Hees, and it is an integral part of their cultural heritage. In fact, Hees has been recognized by UNESCO as an Intangible Cultural Heritage of Humanity, acknowledging its importance in preserving Somali culture and traditions. Some notable Somali poets and Hees masters include: * Sayid Maxamed Cabdille Xasan (Sayid Maxamed Cabdille Xasan) - a renowned Somali poet and Hees master who is considered one of the greatest poets in Somali literature. * Cabdillahi Bulhan (Cabdiqani Bulhan) - a celebrated Somali poet and Hees master who is known for his powerful and emotive poetry. * Maxamed Xaashi Dhamac 'Gaadho' (Maxamed Xaashi Dhamac 'Gaadho') - a prominent Somali poet and Hees master who is recognized for his unique style and mastery of the Hees form. Hees is a testament to the Somali people's rich cultural heritage and their ability to preserve their traditions through art and literature.\", \"source\": \"llm\" }","conversation_id":"1776706813973_z8u83ee"}
